From 0bf9ae01d7f771d3adc38817797e1fc8845f88f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:55:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] infinity6c: map upstream raptor's 0..255 image knobs
 onto native units

Upstream rvd, raptorctl and Thingino's web UI speak raptor's Ingenic scale for
the image knobs: 0..255, with 128 meaning "default". rvd pushes 128 to every
knob at start. John Chia's backend speaks each module's own units, and reports
them through hal_isp_get_knob_caps:
- brightness/contrast/saturation: 0..100
- DRC, defog: 0..255 from 0
- temper: 0..127 around the tuning's value
- ae_comp: signed EV steps

Unmapped, the start-up 128 was rejected by the colour, temper and ae_comp
knobs, and pinned DRC and defog to manual half strength, overriding the
tuning's per-gain curves on every boot.

i6c_upstream_compat.c wraps the 15 knob ops. Each asks for the knob's caps,
maps the value, and calls the native op unchanged:
- 128 leaves the tuning alone: auto, or the neutral for ae_comp, which has
  no auto.
- The upper half maps onto (neutral, max].
- Where 128 is auto, the lower half maps onto [min, neutral], so "manual at
  neutral" stays distinct from auto. That is DRC/defog "off"; reading it
  back as 128 would hand WDR back to the tuning when saved.
- Getters invert the map.

This replaces the probe's clamping getters. tests/t_knob_map_i6c.c is a host
test for five caps profiles: ends, 128, monotonic halves, read-back, and
idempotent round trips.

Also ignore the .build-config stamp.
